# The dev server's log. `npm run dev` must be started detached with its output
# redirected to a file — an attached stdout that stops being read kills Next on
# an uncaught EPIPE, and the process then spins instead of exiting while every
# request hangs. See CLAUDE.md.
dev.log

# 🔓 Real Venmo statements. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC, and a downloaded
# statement carries real payer names, real transaction IDs and real amounts for
# people who never agreed to be in a git history — a third party's name in a
# public repo is not something a later commit can take back.
#
# Keep them locally, never commit one. The fabricated example that IS committed
# is docs/VenmoStatement_August_2026.csv, built entirely from seed members; it
# is what any parser or import work should be developed against.
docs/VenmoStatement_*.csv
!docs/VenmoStatement_August_2026.csv

# UI design skills (docs/install-ui-skills.md, 2026-08-16). Vendored third-party
# skill files — kept local rather than committed. Reinstall with the commands in
# that doc; the precedence rule that governs them IS committed, in CLAUDE.md.
# settings.local.json is machine-local regardless and carries Impeccable's hook.
.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.local.json
skills-lock.json

# 📌 DESIGN.md, PRODUCT.md and .impeccable/design.json are NOT ignored, and that
# is deliberate (2026-08-17). They are Impeccable OUTPUT rather than vendored
# tooling: DESIGN.md is the design source of truth for the whole site, PRODUCT.md
# records the product context and the refusals (no photography, no invented
# statistics), and design.json is the machine sidecar `/impeccable doctor` diffs
# for staleness. Leaving them untracked meant the binding spec existed on one
# laptop. Everything else Impeccable writes under .impeccable/ is session state:
.impeccable/*
!.impeccable/design.json
